---
name: plan-review-task
version: 3.9.0
description: lead plan-review assignment for quality-mgr. task_id is the plan-review bead (<root>-plan-qa), which blocks every sprint container, so nothing is dispatched until the plan passes. The plan is the beads under the root; there is no plan PR.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - root
  - phase
  - round
  - integration_branch
  - plans_dir
  - requirements_globs
  - adr_globs
optional_variables:
  - carry_forward
defaults:
  carry_forward: ""
metadata:
  type: plan-review-task
  tags:
    - stage:plan-review
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: plan-review-start
    stage: plan-review
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" phase="{{ phase }}" mode="plan-review" round="{{ round }}">
  <description><![CDATA[Plan review, round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}, of the beads under `{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}` (phase {{ phase | string | cdata_escape }}). Docs-only: no code, no stack. The beads are the plan.]]></description>

  <root><![CDATA[{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}]]></root>
{% if carry_forward %}  <carry-forward><![CDATA[
{{ carry_forward | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></carry-forward>

  <fix-verification-precedence><![CDATA[A plan review verifying carried findings is not a full plan review. Dispatch only each carried finding's filing reviewer (named on its line). No automatic req-qa/arch-qa, no full plan-scope-reviewer run, no screening panel. Lock scope to the carried findings and their original requirement; no sweep, no new findings. Report fixed/open/regressed for those findings. validate-plan (step b) still runs, like required CI. This rule overrides the broader round-1 instructions in steps c and e.]]></fix-verification-precedence>
{% endif %}
  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Check readiness, claim the bead, then start the review. If blocked, do not claim or start; refuse as in step f (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the exact blocker, the bead or agent that must move, and, for a blocker not yet a dependency, the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[From the repository root, run `.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --root {{ root | string | cdata_escape }}`. Exit 5: each printed problem line is a **blocking** finding, reported exactly as printed. Exit 2: the check could not run; go to step f. Validation checks the plan file and `.atm-bd/phase-<x>.toml`, which must be committed and pushed on the phase's integration branch; a missing artifact is blocking. A `bd doctor` error (a validate-plan warning) is also blocking: the plan is not reviewed against a broken database.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[For each sprint container listed by `bd list --parent {{ root | string | cdata_escape }} -l stage:sprint --all -n 0 --json`, pipe `bd show <bead> --json | jq '.[0] | {id, title, description, design, acceptance_criteria, metadata}'` into `<scratch>/<bead>-plan.md`, inside a fenced json block. Pipe the root the same way into `<scratch>/{{ root | string | cdata_escape }}-plan.md`.
{% if carry_forward %}This is a plan fix round: verify only the carried findings above. Write them to `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.txt` and run `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope owned --plan --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.txt`; it prints each carried finding's filing reviewer with its own finding ids (`<bead> <field>`). Step b re-checks the `validate-plan` ones. Dispatch exactly the other reviewers it prints and no other, after confirming the set with `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope check --plan --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.txt --dispatch <name,...>` (a nonzero exit means the set is wrong: fix it, never dispatch it). Each runs as a background agent on the same piped files (every sprint container file and the root's file), pinned to `{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}` at `git rev-parse origin/{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}`, with `qa_round` = {{ round | string | cdata_escape }} and `carry_forward_findings_json` = its own ids, locked to those findings and the requirement they cite. `plan-scope-reviewer` runs only when it filed a carried finding; render its assignment with `plan-scope-reviewer-assignment.json.j2`: `plan_docs` = every piped sprint container file, `phase_root_doc` = the root's file, `round_index` = {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}, `carry_forward_findings_json` = its own ids (a later round without them refuses to render). Each reports fixed, regressed or open for its own findings and files no new findings.{% else %}Requirements and ADRs are the tight gate. A plan in beads has no branch of its own: pin reviewers to the phase integration branch `{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}` at its current head (`git rev-parse origin/{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}`), which holds the governing documents (requirements: {{ requirements_globs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }}; ADRs: {{ adr_globs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }}). Each of these is a **blocking** finding, never important or minor:
- `metadata.requirements` or `metadata.adrs` is empty, missing, or mixes `NONE` with ids (validate-plan already reports these);
- an id is not in the governing document, unless it meets the New Ids rule of `.claude/skills/atm-beads/resources/planning.md` (the document is in `owned_paths` and a deliverable says the sprint adds the id);
- a listed id does not govern the bead's work;
- the work touches a requirement or ADR the bead does not list, including a bead that says `NONE`.
Run `req-qa` and `arch-qa` as background agents on every piped sprint container file, with `sprint_doc` = that file and the docs-only plan rules of `.claude/agents/quality-mgr.md`. Run `plan-scope-reviewer` over the whole set, in full, its assignment rendered with `plan-scope-reviewer-assignment.json.j2` (`plan_docs` = every piped sprint container file, `phase_root_doc` = the root's file); its `parallelism` numbers go in the report. Run `ceremony-qa` with `review_mode` = `doc_review` and `review_targets` = every piped sprint container file and the root's file. Run the other plan reviewers the docs-only plan rules name on the same piped files, with `qa_round` = {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}.{% endif %}]]></step>
{% if not carry_forward %}    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Run `ceremony-finding-screen` over this round's findings, except the step b findings and the REQ/ADR findings of step c, which are never ceremony. Drop what it screens out and list each drop with its reason in the report.]]></step>
{% endif %}
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Verdict: PASS when no blocking or important finding is open; otherwise FAIL. PASS with no findings: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "plan review PASS round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}"`; closing releases the root sprints. PASS with minor findings: do not close the bead (that would release the root sprints before the fixes); hand it to the task assigner with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --assignee <the task assigner> --append-notes "PASS round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}; minor fixes before dispatch: <list>"`; the assigner applies the fixes and closes it. FAIL: the bead must stay **open** (closing would release them): `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "FAIL round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}: <n> findings"`. Either way, once that `bd` command succeeded, close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/plan-review-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/plan-review-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. Findings live in the report, one line each: `<bead> <severity> <reviewer> <field>: <what is wrong>`, where `<reviewer>` is the agent that filed it (`validate-plan` for step b); a fix round carries these lines and reads its filing reviewers from them.{% if carry_forward %} In this fix round the report lists each carried finding as fixed, regressed or open, plus any step b problem; PASS is every carried finding fixed and step b clean.{% endif %} Do not file finding beads for a plan: the author fixes the beads with `bd update`, and the task assigner assigns the next round.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[If the review cannot run, reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead. Never create a per-task shadow bead or delay the refusal. Also announce a serious infrastructure failure once per cause to the oversight recipients (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role). Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "PLAN_REVIEW_CANNOT_RUN; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. A blocker (a prerequisite reopens, or the work needs a fix that has not landed) is not a failure: stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>"` and close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
